invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_ifma.c
catches: rsa_ifma_model_test
reason: A round keeps all 64 bits of its quotient rather than the low 52.
  VPMADD52LUQ and VPMADD52HUQ read the low 52 bits of each lane, so the
  lanes add quotient mod 2^52 times m while the scalar product by m's
  digit 0 adds the whole quotient, and digit_zero takes m's digit 0
  times the quotient's top 12 bits too much. bin/rsa_ifma_model_test
  compares rsa_vp1_cpu under the bit with rsa_vp1. The record's own mask
  of m0inv is no such check: the low 52 bits of a product depend on the
  low 52 bits of its factors alone, so a quotient taken from an unmasked
  m0inv is the same quotient, and no test can tell the two apart.

--- old
    uint64_t quotient = (uint64_t)ct_mul128((uint64_t)low, modulus->m0inv) & DIGIT_MASK;
--- new
    uint64_t quotient = (uint64_t)ct_mul128((uint64_t)low, modulus->m0inv);
